WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.241
"Lesser Known NAD+ boosting Supplements - Tryptophan, NADH, NMNH, and NRH"

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:10.800
Taking niacin,
also called nicotinic acid,

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.920
would be about 50 times
more efficient

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.400
than taking
the amino acid tryptophan

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.600
to boost NAD+,

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.400
because only about two percent
of tryptophan

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.720
is converted into niacin.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.440
Also, tryptophan didn't work

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.760
to improve mitochondrial
or muscle function

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.320
in physically compromised
older adults,

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.360
even when combined
with niacin or nicotinamide.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.200
And side effects
of taking tryptophan

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.440
include belching and gas,
blurred vision,

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.200
diarrhea, dizziness,
drowsiness, dry mouth,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:37.960
headache, heartburn,

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.480
and potentially
a life-threatening condition

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:44.520
known as eosinophilia-myalgia
syndrome, or EMS.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:48.240
There was an epidemic of EMS
tied to tryptophan supplements

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.960
from a single supplier
back in 1989

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:52.200
that led to their removal

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.520
from the market
for about 15 years.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.000
Some sort of contaminant
was suspected,

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.920
but the cause
remains a mystery.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:01.640
To this day,
tryptophan supplements

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.440
continue to be tainted
with impurities,

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.640
with at least one case
of EMS reported

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:09.200
decades after
the initial epidemic.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.360
A case of EMS tied to
a bizarre weight loss diet

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.240
involving hundreds of cups
(~48 L) of cashews,

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.080
a rich source of tryptophan,

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:18.640
suggests the syndrome
can be caused

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.640
by excess tryptophan directly.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:22.680
If anything,

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.200
tryptophan restriction
may be beneficial.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.120
Nearly 50 years ago,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.160
it was demonstrated
that restricting

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.800
dietary tryptophan
reduced cancer rates

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.840
and increased
the lifespans of rats

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.000
and, subsequently, mice.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.960
Vegetarians and vegans
both appear to have

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.440
significantly lower intakes
of tryptophan,

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.880
but only in vegans
does this translate

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:45.000
to lower
tryptophan blood levels,

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.360
though presumably not

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:50.040
if they were to take
tryptophan supplements.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.800
What about taking NAD+ directly?

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.240
This isn't practical

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.080
because of instability
and poor bioavailability.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:00.920
NAD+ is vulnerable to heat,
pH, light, and oxygen,

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.240
requiring dark desiccant storage

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.760
at ideally 20 degrees (-29°C)
below freezing.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.160
NAD+ can be given intravenously,

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.000
a practice started
in the 1950s

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.000
as an "underground" treatment
for alcoholism,

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.520
but when taken orally,

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:18.160
NAD may be broken down
in the alkaline environment

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.840
of the small intestine,
and NADH,

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.960
the so-called "reduced" form
of NAD+,

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:25.200
is broken down
in the acidic conditions

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.520
of the stomach.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:29.840
(In organic chemistry,
the gain of a hydrogen atom

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.080
is said to quote-unquote
"reduce" the molecule,

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:36.520
so NADH
is the reduced form of NAD+).

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:39.360
Enteric forms of NAD+
could potentially survive

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:42.600
the digestive tract, but,
with the exception of neurons,

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:46.120
NAD can't cross
into mammalian cells.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.760
This is why
NAD+ precursor supplements,

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:52.120
like NMN and NR,
were developed.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:54.560
Also, there are evidently
(unpublished) data

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:55.800
showing that straight NAD+

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:59.160
can cause severe hyperglycemia
in mice.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.320
Has it been tested in people?

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.120
NAD+ boosting supplements

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.800
have been found
to improve the learning

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.560
and memory of rodent models
of Alzheimer's disease

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.040
in the lab.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:13.360
In 1995, case reports
of apparent benefit of NADH

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.520
for Alzheimer's disease
were published.

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:19.080
By the next year, an open-label
pilot study was published,

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:21.240
suggesting it had
a protective effect,

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:23.240
but without
a placebo control group,

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:25.000
the only conclusion
that could be drawn

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.840
was to study it further,

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:28.440
especially since
a similar study

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:29.400
with the same dose

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.280
over approximately
the same period

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:35.040
found no evidence
of any cognitive effects.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:37.960
There have been
two randomized, double-blind,

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.160
placebo-controlled trials

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:41.680
of NAD precursors
for Alzheimer's.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:44.640
One found no benefit
for memory, attention,

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:47.320
or clinician ratings
of dementia severity,

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:49.240
but did maybe find
less of a drop

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:51.080
in one dementia rating scale

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:54.400
after six months
of 10 milligrams a day of NADH.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.920
The other, a six-month study
of nicotinamide,

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.680
failed to find
any clinical effects.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:03.400
What about trying
NMNH and NRH,

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.560
the reduced forms
of NMN and NR?

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:09.240
They both appear
to boost NAD+ higher

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:11.160
than their
non-reduced counterparts.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:14.560
In vitro,
NMNH can raise NAD+ levels

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:17.120
up to 10 times higher than NMN,

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:21.360
and NRH (also known as
dihydronicotinamide riboside)

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:25.200
is up to about 50 times
more potent than NR.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.080
There are concerns
about stability of NRH

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.080
outside the body,

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:31.360
since it's sensitive to oxygen
and moisture,

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:32.640
but within the body,

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:34.400
NRH may be more stable,

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:36.760
not rapidly devolving
into nicotinamide,

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.520
like NR does
(at least in mouse blood).

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:41.120
However, unlike NR,

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.040
NRH does not appear
to be able

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:47.000
to significantly increase levels
in mouse muscles.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.880
NRH is said to have
a "spectacular potency"

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:51.600
for increasing NAD+ levels,

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:55.000
perhaps the most potent
precursor discovered to date.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.680
This may not necessarily be
a good thing.

00:04:57.680 --> 00:04:59.560
The extreme boost
afforded by NRH

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:04.080
had detrimental consequences
in human liver cells in vitro,

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.240
resulting from
an excessive accumulation

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:07.600
of free radicals.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:08.640
In addition to oxidation,

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:11.840
NRH was also found
promote inflammation.

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:14.080
Pro-inflammatory effects
were noted for NRH

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:19.400
on human immune cells in vitro
(but not for NMN, NAM, or NR).

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:22.680
Because it appears that NMNH
is converted to NRH

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.120
to enter cells,

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:26.120
these potentially
deleterious effects

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:28.480
may be shared
by NMNH as well

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:46.720
(though this has yet
to be tested).

